# 3. Power Set Using Bit Masking

```java
List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();

int n = str.length();

for(int mask = 0; mask < (1 << n); mask++) {

    StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();

    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {

        if((mask & (1 << i)) != 0) {
            sb.append(str.charAt(i));
        }
    }

    list.add(sb.toString());
}
```

Time Complexity: O(n × 2ⁿ)

